   "notes": "I describe BERT-BASE as the primary config; BERT-LARGE is also listed. Attention heads in block_ops use BASE values (16 for LARGE), as does the FFN width (4096 for LARGE). The block structure (post-LN LayerNorm, residuals) is marked inherited from the Transformer of Vaswani et al., based on the 'almost identical to the original' sentence; the paper does not restate it. The paper says 'gelu' but not whether it is the exact or tanh form, so the gelu op's approx is not_stated. Left not_stated: head_dim (64 is implied by H/A but never written), n_kv_heads, LayerNorm eps, biases, an embedding LayerNorm or dropout placement in the architecture, and tying of the output layer. The size-ablation models in Table 6 are ablations, not the paper's model configs."
